(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase459LanguageCompactionAndPredictability"
  :createdAt 1789160000000
  :status "done"
  :priorityOrder 1
  :summary "Language Compaction and Predictability: one name per concept, the measured 3.38 percent of syntax compaction actually available, opaque aliases retired at a deliberate token cost, and symbol surface tracked as the quantity that governs model accuracy."
  :phase "Phase459LanguageCompactionAndPredictability"
  :baseline "Measured 2026-09-11 over 888 ASL files, 5632473 characters, 1512691 cl100k tokens at 3.72 characters per token. String literals are 41.8 percent of all tokens and no syntax change reaches them. Docstrings are 6.7 percent, type signatures 1.0 percent, module headers 3.4 percent. Common head symbols already cost one token each: assert 8668 uses, df 6887, let 5263, if 3011. Of 921 declared import aliases 66 percent are one or two characters, the alias s is declared in 76 files, and 11.7 percent of the 11132 qualified uses sit more than 200 lines from the declaration that binds them, median 53 and maximum 1172. 17112 distinct head symbols appear in call position against 6966 defined names. The same concept carries several sanctioned spellings: 337 predicates end in a question mark while 227 start with is and 192 do both; constructors split across make 388, build 42, create 38 and new 3; conversions split across X-to-Y 154, X-from-Y 18, to-X 4 and as-X 1. Total compaction available from every syntax change combined is 3.38 percent: renaming the 14 most expensive builtins 0.97 percent, collapsing the predicate forms 0.09 percent, CamelCase across all 18267 hyphenated identifiers 3.06 percent, less 0.74 percent spent on legible aliases."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task45901"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-459"
      :title "One name per concept, decided before any new builtin is written"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "naming"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "planner"
      :createdAt 1789160000000
      :updatedAt 1789421200000
      :motivation "A model predicting how to ask whether a value is a thing finds three sanctioned answers in this corpus: 337 names end in a question mark, 227 begin with is, and 192 do both. Constructors carry four prefixes and conversions four shapes. Each variant is individually defensible and collectively they mean the model must memorise this repository rather than generalise from the languages it has read. This is not a token problem, it is an accuracy problem, and it compounds: Task45403 is about to add 40 new builtins, and writing them before the convention is settled bakes the fragmentation into the primitives themselves."
      :purpose "One spelling per concept, recorded in the grammar rather than in prose: a predicate ends in a question mark and never begins with is, a constructor is make followed by the type, a conversion is source-to-target. A checker rejects a definition that uses a retired form, and the 40 builtins of Task45403 are named from this decision rather than from habit."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["One sanctioned form per concept in the grammar" "419 predicate names and 83 constructor names converged" "A checker that rejects retired forms" "Task45403 names its 40 builtins from this decision"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/language-semantics.asn" "asl/grammar/grammar.asn" "TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md"]
      :targetSymbols ["is-" "make-" "create-" "build-"]
      :relatedSymbols ["names" "semantics" "concepts"]
      :invariants ["D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn []
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45901"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45901.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A definition named is-empty is rejected and the message names the sanctioned form." "A definition named is-empty? is rejected, because carrying both markers is the most common current variant." "A predicate correctly named empty? passes." "The check runs over the grammar registries as well as over sources, so a retired form cannot be reintroduced by declaration."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45901" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define predicateNaming semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task45901-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Decide one form per concept." "Record it in the grammar." "Add the checker." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task45901-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task45902"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-459"
      :title "Rename the 14 measured expensive builtins"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "compaction"
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789160000000
      :updatedAt 1789421800000
      :motivation "Frequency times cost identifies the primitives worth renaming and rules out the rest. string-contains? costs 4 tokens and is called 2754 times, string-starts-with? costs 5 and is called 621, string-from-int64 costs 4 and is called 613. Fourteen such names account for 14712 tokens, 0.97 percent of the corpus. Everything else in the head position already costs one token, so there is nothing further to win there and no case for a general abbreviation campaign."
      :purpose "The fourteen are renamed to their shortest form that stays unambiguous under the Task45901 convention, with the old names removed rather than aliased, because an alias keeps both spellings alive and that is the condition this phase exists to end."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["14 names renamed, old spellings removed" "0.97 percent measured, recorded with its method" "No compatibility aliases left behind"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/language-semantics.asn" "asl/tools/engine_js.h"]
      :targetSymbols ["string-contains?" "string-starts-with?" "string-from-int64" "string-replace" "list-length"]
      :relatedSymbols ["names" "output"]
      :invariants ["D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45901"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45902"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45902.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A retired spelling fails rather than resolving through an alias." "The measured saving is recomputed from the tree after the rename and matches the prediction within a stated tolerance." "No renamed primitive collides with an existing name."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45902" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define expensiveBuiltinsRenamed semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task45902-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Rank by frequency times cost." "Rename the fourteen." "Recompute and record." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task45902-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task45903"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-459"
      :title "CamelCase for multi-word identifiers, at the corpus-wide figure"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "compaction"
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789160000000
      :updatedAt 1789422400000
      :motivation "4398 of 6966 defined names carry three or more words, and hyphenated identifiers are 20.4 percent of all corpus tokens at 3.19 tokens per occurrence against 2.58 for CamelCase. Only 4.0 percent of identifier occurrences are CamelCase today, so D51 is declared and barely applied. Converting every hyphenated identifier saves 46259 tokens, which is 3.06 percent of the corpus: real, and the largest single item available, and an order of magnitude below the 20 to 50 percent the convention document states."
      :purpose "Multi-word identifiers are CamelCase, applied by a transformation over the tree rather than by hand, and the saving is measured on the tree before and after rather than extrapolated from example lines."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Multi-word identifiers converted mechanically" "Before and after measured on the whole corpus" "The conversion is reversible and reviewable as one change per file"]
      :owns ["asl/packages" "harness/src" "intel/src" "mem/src" "agent-core/src" "vdom/src"]
      :targetSymbols []
      :relatedSymbols ["names" "output"]
      :invariants ["D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45901" "Task45601"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45903"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45903.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Executed assertion count is unchanged across the conversion, so the rename did not silently unbind anything." "An identifier inside a string literal is not rewritten." "The recorded saving is computed, not quoted from the plan."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45903" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define assertionParityAcrossTransformations semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task45903-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Transform mechanically." "Measure before and after." "Confirm assertion parity." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task45903-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task45904"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-459"
      :title "Retire opaque aliases and pay the 0.74 percent"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "predictability"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789160000000
      :updatedAt 1789423000000
      :motivation "246 of 921 declared aliases are a single character and 362 are two. The alias s is declared in 76 different files and means a different module in each. A reader, human or model, cannot interpret s/concat without locating the header that binds it, and 11.7 percent of the 11132 qualified uses sit more than 200 lines from that header, with a maximum of 1172 and a median of 53. A model reading a slice of a file, which is how every retrieval path in this repository works, sees the use and not the binding. This is the cost of the compaction style the convention document holds up as canonical."
      :purpose "A qualified prefix is legible on its own: at least three characters, derived from the module it names, and meaning one module across the whole corpus. Where the module already has a short declared name the alias is omitted entirely and that name is the prefix, so there is no binding to find. The measured cost of about 11132 extra tokens, 0.74 percent, is accepted deliberately and recorded as such."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["No alias shorter than three characters" "One meaning per prefix across the corpus" "Aliases omitted where the module name serves" "The 0.74 percent cost recorded as a decision, not an accident"]
      :owns ["asl/packages" "harness/src" "agent-bus/src" "intel/src" "mem/src" "voice/src"]
      :targetSymbols []
      :relatedSymbols ["context" "bounded" "names"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D34" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45402"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45904"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45904.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A two character alias is rejected." "One prefix bound to two different modules anywhere in the corpus is rejected, naming both." "A file whose qualified uses all resolve without reading its header passes, which is the property being bought."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45904" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define legibleAliasLength semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task45904-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Assign one legible prefix per module." "Rewrite uses." "Add the uniqueness check." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task45904-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task45905"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-459"
      :title "Symbol surface as the tracked quantity, above token count"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "predictability"
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "planner"
      :createdAt 1789160000000
      :updatedAt 1789423600000
      :motivation "17112 distinct symbols appear in head position across 1512691 tokens, about one distinct symbol for every 88 tokens of corpus. A model working in this language must carry that surface, and it has almost no pretraining exposure to any of it. Published multi-language results put a low resource Lisp far below Python on the same tasks, which is a difference in familiarity rather than in syntax, and no amount of shortening changes it. Meanwhile every syntax change available here totals 3.38 percent. The project has been optimising the quantity that barely moves and not measuring the one that governs the outcome."
      :purpose "Distinct symbol surface is recorded in the same inventory as token count and is the quantity a language proposal must argue against. A change that reduces tokens while increasing surface, or while increasing distance between a binding and its uses, is rejected unless it carries evidence that accuracy did not fall."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Symbol surface tracked alongside token count" "Language proposals evaluated on both" "A token saving that costs legibility is rejected by default" "The measured basis for the trade recorded with source and scope"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/rules.asn" ".asl/mem/telemetry" "TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md"]
      :targetSymbols []
      :relatedSymbols ["concepts" "names" "context" "ssot"]
      :invariants ["D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45704"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45905"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45905.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Adding a synonym for an existing primitive raises the tracked surface and fails the ratchet." "A proposal reducing tokens while raising surface is rejected without accuracy evidence." "The inventory reports both quantities from one run."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45905" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define symbolSurfaceTracking semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task45905-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Add surface to the inventory." "Ratchet it." "Record the trade rule." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task45905-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task45906"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-459"
      :title "Correct the D51 claim to its measured scope"
      :kind :protocol
      :state :completed
      :lane "naming"
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789160000000
      :updatedAt 1789423900000
      :motivation "TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md and the names rule state a 20 to 50 percent reduction from CamelCase. Measured against the identifiers the document cites, that is exact: the two worked examples reproduce at 50.0 and 44.4 percent. Measured across the corpus the same change is 3.06 percent, because most identifiers are one or two words and 41.8 percent of tokens are string literals that no naming convention reaches. A figure true of an example and false of the system is the failure mode the concepts rule was adopted to prevent, and it is currently the headline number of the project's own convention document."
      :purpose "The claim carries its scope, its method and its corpus-wide figure: per long identifier 44 to 50 percent, corpus-wide 3.06 percent, measured on 888 files under cl100k on a stated date. The same treatment is applied to every other number in the document."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Per-identifier and corpus-wide figures both stated" "Method and date recorded" "Every remaining number in the document carries source and scope"]
      :owns ["TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md" "asl/grammar/rules.asn" "AGENTS.md"]
      :targetSymbols ["names"]
      :relatedSymbols ["concepts" "ssot"]
      :invariants ["D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45903"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45906"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45906.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A number in the document without scope and method fails the check." "The stated corpus-wide figure is reproducible by command on the tree it names." "The rule surface rendered to every client carries the corrected claim."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45906" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define groundedNumericClaims semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task45906-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Recompute each stated number." "Attach scope and method." "Render to every surface." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task45906-verified-20260912"])]
  :notes "The finding that shapes this phase is that the language is already compact. Head symbols cost one token, keywords cost one token, type signatures are 1.0 percent and string literals are 41.8 percent and unreachable. Everything syntax can still win totals 3.38 percent, while the quantity that plausibly governs model accuracy, distinct symbol surface and the distance between a binding and its use, has never been measured or tracked. Task45901 must precede Task45403, which is about to add 40 primitives.")
